            part2Content = "Exact Equations & Governing Rules:\n• K-Means Centroid Update: μ_k = (1 / |C_k|) ∑ x_i\n• Silhouette Formula: s(i) = (b(i) - a(i)) / max(a(i), b(i))\n• PCA Projection: Z = X V_k (where V_k contains top k eigenvectors of X^T X)\n\nWorked Numerical Example:\nProblem: Cluster 4 points on a 1D line: x₁ = 2, x₂ = 4, x₃ = 10, x₄ = 12 using K-Means with K = 2 and initial centroids μ₁ = 3, μ₂ = 9.\nStep 1: Assignment Step (Assign each point to nearest centroid):\n• Point x₁ = 2: |2 - 3| = 1, |2 - 9| = 7 ⇒ Assigned to C₁.\n• Point x₂ = 4: |4 - 3| = 1, |4 - 9| = 5 ⇒ Assigned to C₁.\n• Point x₃ = 10: |10 - 3| = 7, |10 - 9| = 1 ⇒ Assigned to C₂.\n• Point x₄ = 12: |12 - 3| = 9, |12 - 9| = 3 ⇒ Assigned to C₂.\nPartition: C₁ = {2, 4}, C₂ = {10, 12}.\nStep 2: Update Step (Recompute centroids as means):\n• New μ₁ = (2 + 4) / 2 = 6 / 2 = 3.0.\n• New μ₂ = (10 + 12) / 2 = 22 / 2 = 11.0.\nStep 3: Second Assignment Step with μ₁ = 3.0, μ₂ = 11.0:\n• x₁ = 2: |2-3|=1 vs |2-11|=9 ⇒ C₁.\n• x₂ = 4: |4-3|=1 vs |4-11|=7 ⇒ C₁.\n• x₃ = 10: |10-3|=7 vs |10-11|=1 ⇒ C₂.\n• x₄ = 12: |12-3|=9 vs |12-11|=1 ⇒ C₂.\nConclusion: Cluster assignments are unchanged; centroids have converged at μ₁ = 3.0 and μ₂ = 11.0.\n\nReal-World Applications:\nUnsupervised learning is vital for big data discovery. E-commerce platforms use K-Means for customer segmentation (grouping users by purchase history). Cybersecurity intrusion detection systems use DBSCAN to isolate anomalous network traffic spikes as noise outliers. Genomic research uses PCA and UMAP to reduce millions of gene expression dimensions into 2D cluster maps.",
            examTip = "University Exam Tip: K-Means assumes spherical clusters of equal variance and is extremely sensitive to outliers. DBSCAN can find arbitrary non-spherical shapes (such as concentric circles) and automatically labels outliers as noise without forcing them into a cluster.",
